  4.00    0.50677     33.13       136.467     0.8388      879.1     0.357    1.939

  LOCAL EXPONENT BETWEEN CONSECUTIVE RUNGS
  k range        bias->rate   rate->cent   cent->F1   
  0.25 -> 0.50    0.21         0.65         1.00        <- where the LEARNED bias lives
  0.50 -> 1.00    0.69         0.51         1.00      
  1.00 -> 2.00    1.42         0.14         1.00      
  2.00 -> 4.00    1.12         -0.00        1.00      

  end to end, first rung to last   0.17  (product 0.17)
  centroid                         0.7110 -> 0.8388, and it SATURATES
  pinned share                     0.000 -> 0.357

  IN THE LEARNED REGIME the compressive stage is `bias -> rate` at 0.21, against
  0.65 for the other. Over the WHOLE ladder that inverts, because the
  centroid saturates near its bound at high k -- a regime only an oracle
  reaches, and reporting one fit across both would name the wrong stage.

  SO THE TARGET IS THE NEURON, NOT THE POOLING. `bias -> rate` is the
  drive-to-rate transfer, and at the magnitudes reward can reach it is
  already sublinear -- which is why `poolbeta` sharpened the POOLING and
  bought convergence speed rather than ceiling. It was attacking the stage
  that is NOT compressive where the learned bias lives.
  [stageprobe took 140.5 s]

